const CONNECTIONS = [["indian-indentured-labour-in-natal","mahatma-gandhi","That brought a young lawyer, [[mahatma-gandhi|Mohandas Gandhi]], into politics after he arrived in 1893; he helped found the [[natal-indian-congress|Natal Indian Congress]] in 1894."],["juan-pablo-perez-alfonzo","opec-founded","He worked with the Saudi oil minister Abdullah Tariki to bring the big exporters together, and in September 1960 they founded the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries, [[opec-founded|OPEC]], in Baghdad."],["marcus-garvey","kwame-nkrumah","His ideas shaped [[pan-africanism|Pan-Africanism]] and leaders such as [[kwame-nkrumah|Kwame Nkrumah]], and the followers of [[rastafari|Rastafari]] saw him as a prophet."],["mahatma-gandhi","martin-luther-king-jr","His methods later shaped [[martin-luther-king-jr|Martin Luther King Jr.]] and [[nelson-mandela|Nelson Mandela]]."],["pasai-first-muslim-sultanate","ibn-battuta","The traveller [[ibn-battuta|Ibn Battuta]] stopped there in 1345 and 1346 on his way to China and described a Muslim sultan who loved debating religious law."],["potosi-silver","ming","Much of it ended up in China, which wanted silver to pay taxes under the [[ming|Ming]], carried either through Europe and India or across the Pacific on the [[manila-galleons|Manila galleons]]."],["rongorongo","cuneiform","If it is writing made on the island, it is one of the very few independent inventions of writing, with [[cuneiform|cuneiform]], [[chinese-characters|Chinese]] and [[maya-script|Maya script]]."],["mark-twain","philippine-american-war","He became a world famous lecturer and a sharp critic of imperialism, opposing the US war in the [[philippine-american-war|Philippines]]."],["university-of-bologna","nalanda","Older centres of higher learning existed elsewhere, such as [[nalanda|Nalanda]] in India, [[university-of-al-qarawiyyin|al-Qarawiyyin]] in Fez and the [[university-of-constantinople|University of Constantinople]], but Bologna's self-governing body that grants degrees is the ancestor of the modern university."],["ibn-battuta","delhi-sultanate","In India he [[ibn-battuta-reaches-delhi|reached Delhi]] and served the sultan of the [[delhi-sultanate|Delhi Sultanate]] as a judge for years."],["sargon-of-akkad","meluhha-trade-with-sumer","Sargon ruled through governors and a standing army, and boasted that ships from [[dilmun|Dilmun]] and [[meluhha-trade-with-sumer|Meluhha]] docked at Akkad."],["first-battle-of-panipat","ottoman-empire","He chained carts together to make a wall, with gaps for his field guns and matchlock men, a method the [[ottoman-empire|Ottomans]] used."],["arpanet","sputnik-1","It was paid for by ARPA, a research agency of the US Department of Defense set up in 1958 in response to [[sputnik-1|Sputnik]]."],["ghana-wagadu","al-khwarizmi","When it began is unknown; the first written mention comes from the Baghdad scholar [[al-khwarizmi|al-Khwarizmi]] around 830, and its origins may go back to about 300."],["tambora-eruption","cholera-pandemic-from-bengal","Some historians link the disrupted monsoon to the [[cholera-pandemic-from-bengal|cholera outbreak in Bengal]] in 1817, though the connection is not proven."],["bose-statistics","albert-einstein","A journal turned his paper down, so he sent it to [[albert-einstein|Albert Einstein]]."],["hyksos","kerma","The Hyksos king Apepi courted an alliance with [[kerma|Kerma]] in Nubia against Thebes."],["unified-payments-interface","m-pesa","It is part of the digital public infrastructure India built on [[aadhaar|Aadhaar]] identity numbers, and other countries have studied it, much as they once studied Kenya's [[m-pesa|M-Pesa]]."],["araniko","yuan","A Newar artist and architect from the Kathmandu valley in [[nepal|Nepal]], born in 1245, who rose to lead the imperial workshops of the [[yuan|Yuan dynasty]] in China."],["california-gold-rush","victorian-gold-rush","Gold seekers moved on to new rushes, such as the [[victorian-gold-rush|Victorian gold rush]] in Australia from 1851."],["great-exhibition","first-anglo-sikh-war","The [[koh-i-noor|Koh-i-Noor]] diamond, taken from the Punjab after the [[first-anglo-sikh-war|Sikh wars]], was one of the stars, though visitors were underwhelmed by its dull cut, and it was later recut."],["pallavas","xuanzang","Kanchipuram was a centre of learning in Sanskrit and Tamil, for Hindus, Buddhists and Jains. The Chinese pilgrim [[xuanzang|Xuanzang]] visited around 640."],["bowring-treaty","first-opium-war","King [[mongkut|Mongkut]] had watched Britain force open China in the [[first-opium-war|Opium War]]."],["muhammad-iqbal","rumi","He took [[rumi|Rumi]] as his guide and wrote in Persian partly to reach readers across the Islamic world."],["guano-era","coolie-trade","The digging was brutal work, done by convicts and, increasingly, [[coolie-trade|Chinese indentured workers]] brought on harsh contracts."],["sugar-plantations-of-sao-tome","portuguese-brazil","Revolts such as [[rei-amador|Amador's]], raids and competition from [[portuguese-brazil|Brazil]] ended the boom by about 1600, but the system of mill, plantation and slave labour it tested shaped the Americas."],["the-great-wave-off-kanagawa","vincent-van-gogh","Painters such as [[vincent-van-gogh|Van Gogh]], Monet and Degas collected them and copied their flat colours, bold outlines and unusual angles, and the first edition of Debussy's La Mer put it on the cover."],["java-man","charles-darwin","The Dutch doctor [[eugene-dubois|Eugène Dubois]] went to the Dutch East Indies as an army surgeon for one purpose: to find the \"missing link\" between apes and humans that followers of [[charles-darwin|Darwin]] expected in Asia."],["haile-selassie","rastafari","The [[rastafari|Rastafari]] movement, born in Jamaica, sees him as divine; he granted land to Rastafari settlers in the [[shashamane-land-grant|Shashamane land grant]]."],["maurya-empire","seleucid-empire","Around 305 BCE he fought and then made a treaty with Alexander's general [[seleucid-empire|Seleucus]], gaining Afghanistan and Baluchistan in return for 500 war elephants."],["joachimsthaler-coin","potosi-silver","The word then moved to the Spanish silver peso, the [[spanish-dollar|Spanish dollar]], minted from American silver such as [[potosi-silver|Potosí]]."],["han-census","roman-empire","The [[roman-empire|Roman Empire]] of the same years probably had a similar number of people."],["belitung-shipwreck","abbasid-caliphate","Some bowls bear Arabic style patterns and Quranic phrases, made to suit buyers in the [[abbasid-caliphate|Abbasid]] world."],["sukhothai-ayutthaya","vijayanagara","European visitors in the early 16th century ranked it with [[vijayanagara|Vijayanagara]] and Ming China as one of the three great powers of Asia."],["rumi","mongol-empire","As the [[mongol-empire|Mongols]] advanced they fled west, and after years on the road they settled in Konya, capital of the [[seljuk-caliphate|Sultanate of Rum]]."],["melbourne-olympics","hungarian-revolution-of-1956","The Netherlands, Spain and Switzerland stayed away in protest at the Soviet crushing of the [[hungarian-revolution-of-1956|Hungarian revolution]]."],["idris-alooma","ottoman-empire","Ruling from Ngazargamu in what is now northeastern Nigeria, he hired Turkish musketeers and bought firearms through the [[ottoman-empire|Ottoman]] lands to the north, among the first such weapons in the region."],["tazara-railway","china-republic-then-peoples-republic","A railway of about 1,860 kilometres from the port of [[dar-es-salaam|Dar es Salaam]] in Tanzania to Kapiri Mposhi in central [[zambia|Zambia]], built from 1970 to 1975 by the [[china-republic-then-peoples-republic|People's Republic of China]]."],["capture-of-guam-1898","spanish-american-war","The Spanish governor, who had not heard that the [[spanish-american-war|Spanish-American War]] had begun, came out to apologise for not returning the salute, and was told he was a prisoner."],["son-cubano","congolese-rumba","Congolese [[congolese-rumba|rumba]] grew from Cuban son records played in Africa, and son lies under much of [[merengue-music|Caribbean]] dance music."],["dutch-east-india-company","dejima","It was the only European trader allowed in Japan, at [[dejima|Dejima]] in Nagasaki, from 1641."],["madhavas-infinite-series","isaac-newton","These results came about 250 years before Gregory, [[gottfried-wilhelm-leibniz|Leibniz]] and [[isaac-newton|Newton]] found the same series in Europe."],["cherokee-syllabary","hangul-created","It is one of the very few times one person invented a full writing system from nothing, like the Korean [[hangul-created|hangul]] made by a royal team."],["cassava-reaches-central-africa","portuguese-brazil","The bitter kinds hold poison and must be soaked, dried or fermented, and African cooks learned the methods, probably from [[portuguese-brazil|Brazil]]."],["doctrina-christiana","printing-press-in-mexico","Printing reached Manila half a century after the [[printing-press-in-mexico|printing press in Mexico]], since the [[philippines|Philippines]] were ruled through New Spain."],["w-arthur-lewis","nobel-prize","He taught at Princeton. With [[derek-walcott|Derek Walcott]], he gave tiny St Lucia two [[nobel-prize|Nobel prizes]]."],["simon-bolivar","french-revolution","In Rome in 1805 he swore to free his homeland, inspired by the Enlightenment and by the [[us-declaration-of-independence|American]] and [[french-revolution|French]] revolutions."],["jantar-mantar-jaipur","ulugh-begs-observatory","He studied Islamic astronomy, including the tables of [[ulugh-beg|Ulugh Beg]] made at [[ulugh-begs-observatory|Samarkand]], and Sanskrit works, and had European books brought to him."],["aime-cesaire","leopold-sedar-senghor","As a student in Paris in the 1930s he worked with [[leopold-sedar-senghor|Leopold Sedar Senghor]] and Leon Damas to assert the worth of Black and African culture."],["w-arthur-lewis","kwame-nkrumah","He advised the new government of Ghana under [[kwame-nkrumah|Kwame Nkrumah]], headed the University of the West Indies and founded the Caribbean Development Bank."],["le-quy-don","qing","In 1760 he went as envoy to [[qing|Qing]] China, where he talked with Chinese scholars and Korean envoys and read new books, including some on European science brought by Jesuits."],["subrahmanyan-chandrasekhar","manhattan-project","His skill in the physics of fluids led [[j-robert-oppenheimer|Robert Oppenheimer]] to invite him to join the [[manhattan-project|Manhattan Project]] at Los Alamos."],["chola-empire","song","The Cholas sent embassies to [[song|Song]] China, and Tamil merchant guilds traded across the Bay of Bengal."],["indian-ocean-tsunami","sri-lankan-civil-war","In Aceh, the disaster helped bring a peace deal between rebels and the government in 2005; in Sri Lanka, quarrels over aid deepened the [[sri-lankan-civil-war|civil war]]."],["sweet-potato-reaches-china","manila-galleons","Spanish ships carried it across the Pacific to the Philippines on the [[manila-galleons|Manila galleons]]."],["settlement-of-madagascar","austronesians-reach-the-philippines","The voyage was part of the long Austronesian expansion that began when farmers and sailors [[austronesians-reach-the-philippines|moved south from Taiwan to the Philippines]] around 2200 BCE."],["kush-napata-meroe","roman-empire","Queens called Kandake held real power; one negotiated with the [[roman-empire|Roman Empire]] after a war in the 20s BCE."],["slavery-abolition-act","indian-indenture-in-the-caribbean","To replace freed workers, planters soon turned to [[indian-indenture-in-the-caribbean|indentured labourers from India]], and [[slavery-at-the-cape|slavery at the Cape]] gave way to new forms of control."],["ayyubid-mamluk-egypt","mansa-musas-pilgrimage","[[mansa-musas-pilgrimage|Mansa Musa]] passed through in 1324 and spent so much gold that its price fell."],["tibetan-self-immolations","buddhist-crisis","Their form recalls the protest of the Vietnamese monk [[thich-quang-duc|Thich Quang Duc]] in 1963, during the [[buddhist-crisis|Buddhist crisis]]."],["menelik-ii","italy","The [[treaty-of-wuchale|Treaty of Wuchale]] of 1889 with [[italy|Italy]] had a clause that Italy read as making Ethiopia a protectorate."],["assam-tea-plant-found","first-opium-war","At the time Britain bought all its tea from China and paid with silver, and later with opium, which led toward the [[first-opium-war|First Opium War]]."],["taung-child","charles-darwin","Dart argued it was a human ancestor and that humans had evolved in Africa, as [[charles-darwin|Charles Darwin]] had guessed."],["gulf-migration-from-kerala","1973-oil-embargo","When oil prices jumped after the [[1973-oil-embargo|1973 oil embargo]], Gulf states such as [[saudi-arabia|Saudi Arabia]], the [[united-arab-emirates|United Arab Emirates]] and [[kuwait|Kuwait]] began to build fast and needed workers."],["ile-sainte-marie","golden-age-of-piracy","The pirates' attacks on the Mughal ships helped push [[east-india-company|European trading companies]] and navies to police the [[indian-ocean-trade-at-full-reach|Indian Ocean]], ending the [[golden-age-of-piracy|golden age of piracy]]."],["union-miniere-du-haut-katanga","manhattan-project","Its [[shinkolobwe|Shinkolobwe]] mine supplied much of the uranium for the American [[manhattan-project|Manhattan Project]] in the Second World War."],["dutch-conquest-of-banda","treaty-of-breda-1667","The English held on to tiny Run island until the [[treaty-of-breda-1667|Treaty of Breda]] of 1667, when it was left to the Dutch while England kept New Amsterdam, later New York."],["jikji","gutenberg-bible","It is the oldest surviving book printed with movable metal type, older than the [[gutenberg-bible|Gutenberg Bible]] by about 78 years."],["tripitaka-koreana","mongol-empire","The court, which had fled to Ganghwa Island, ordered a new set, hoping that the merit of the work would bring the Buddha's protection against the [[mongol-empire|Mongol Empire]]."],["caodaism","sun-yat-sen","They also venerate saints from outside Asia, most famously the French writer [[victor-hugo|Victor Hugo]], along with [[sun-yat-sen|Sun Yat-sen]]."],["great-trek","slavery-abolition-act","They left because they resented British rule: the end of slavery under the [[slavery-abolition-act|Slavery Abolition Act]], too little protection on the frontier, and English laws and language."],["mozambican-war-of-independence","carnation-revolution","The war, with those in Angola and Guinea-Bissau, drained Portugal and led to the [[carnation-revolution|Carnation Revolution]] in Lisbon in April 1974."],["licchavis-of-nepal","songtsen-gampo","Tradition says a Licchavi princess, Bhrikuti, married the Tibetan king [[songtsen-gampo|Songtsen Gampo]]."],["pallavas","khmer-script","Their form of the south Indian Grantha script was taken up in Southeast Asia and grew into the scripts of Cambodia, Java and other lands, including the [[khmer-script|Khmer script]]."],["funan","roman-empire","The port of [[oc-eo|Óc Eo]], dug up in the 1940s, has yielded Indian jewellery, Chinese bronze mirrors and even Roman coins of the [[roman-empire|Roman Empire]]."],["atisha","srivijaya","Tradition says he sailed to Suvarnadvipa, in the [[srivijaya|Srivijaya]] realm of Sumatra, and studied for twelve years under a master there."],["caral-supe","old-kingdom-egypt","For scale: it rose about a thousand years after the [[sumerian-city-states|Sumerian city-states]], at the same time as the pyramids of [[old-kingdom-egypt|Old Kingdom Egypt]], and nearly two thousand years before the [[olmec-centres|Olmecs]] of Mexico."],["north-korean-famine","soviet-union-dissolves","When the [[soviet-union-dissolves|Soviet Union dissolved]] in 1991, that help ended, and China cut its aid too."],["nine-chapters-on-mathematics","euclid","Unlike [[euclid|Euclid]]'s Elements, it seeks general methods rather than proofs."],["sea-venture","william-shakespeare","Their story reached London and is thought to have inspired [[william-shakespeare|Shakespeare]] in [[the-tempest|The Tempest]]."],["dome-of-the-rock","eastern-roman-byzantine-empire","The design is borrowed. The octagon plan, the dome on a drum and the gold glass mosaics follow the churches of the [[eastern-roman-byzantine-empire|Byzantine Empire]], and local Christian craftsmen probably did much of the work."],["ahmad-al-mansur","songhai-empire","In 1591 he sent an army with guns across the Sahara, which defeated the [[songhai-empire|Songhai Empire]] at the [[battle-of-tondibi|Battle of Tondibi]] and took Timbuktu and Gao."],["lebanese-emigration","brazil","Large communities grew in [[brazil|Brazil]], [[argentina|Argentina]], [[mexico|Mexico]], the United States and [[senegal|Senegal]] and other parts of West Africa."],["persian-famine-of-1870-to-1872","american-civil-war","During the [[american-civil-war|American Civil War]] cotton prices had soared, and many farmers had moved from grain to cotton and opium, which could be sold abroad."],["henry-kissingers-secret-trip-to-china","bangladesh-genocide","It also had a cost. Washington's need for Yahya's help is one reason it stayed silent over the [[bangladesh-genocide|killings in Bangladesh]]."],["pala-empire","srivijaya","A king of [[srivijaya|Srivijaya]] in Sumatra paid for a monastery at Nalanda, and Devapala granted villages for its upkeep."],["an-lushan-rebellion","uyghur-khaganate","The Tang won only with the help of troops from the [[uyghur-khaganate|Uyghur Khaganate]]."],["mahmud-al-kashgari","seljuk-empire","At that time the Turkic [[seljuk-empire|Seljuks]] ruled Baghdad, and he wanted Arabs to learn the language of the new masters."],["mrauk-u","bengal-sultanate","The kingdom was founded by King Min Saw Mon, who had spent years in exile at the court of the [[bengal-sultanate|Bengal Sultanate]] and came back with its help."],["eddington-experiment","albert-einstein","Their plates showed the stars shifted by about the amount [[albert-einstein|Einstein's]] general theory of relativity predicted, rather than the smaller amount from [[isaac-newton|Newton's]] physics."],["things-fall-apart","w-b-yeats","He wrote in English, while working at the Nigerian Broadcasting Corporation, and took the title from a line in [[w-b-yeats|W. B. Yeats]]'s poem \"The Second Coming\"."],["muziris","pliny-the-elder","Greek and Latin writers, from the Periplus to [[pliny-the-elder|Pliny the Elder]], name it."],["black-july","canada","It also began a large exodus that built the [[sri-lankan-tamil-diaspora|Tamil diaspora]] in [[canada|Canada]], Britain and Europe."],["prussian-compulsory-schooling","modern-japan","The American Horace Mann praised it in the 1840s, and it shaped public schools in the United States, the rest of [[germany|Germany]], Scandinavia and [[modern-japan|Meiji Japan]]."],["ushahidi","haiti-earthquake","After the [[haiti-earthquake|2010 Haiti earthquake]] volunteers used Ushahidi to map calls for help, and it has since tracked elections, floods, wildfires and outbreaks around the world."],["harun-al-rashid","charlemagne-crowned-emperor","He also exchanged embassies with [[charlemagne-crowned-emperor|Charlemagne]] and sent him an elephant."],["sack-of-rome","augustine-of-hippo","[[augustine-of-hippo|Augustine]] wrote The City of God partly to answer pagans who blamed the disaster on Christianity."],["indonesia-declares-independence","atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki","With Japan beaten after the [[atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki|atomic bombings]] and the Soviet entry into the war, young radicals pressed Sukarno and Hatta to act before the Allies arrived."],["siege-of-muscat-1650","fort-jesus","Omani fleets chased the Portuguese down the East African coast and took [[fort-jesus|Fort Jesus]] at Mombasa in 1698."],["siam-abolishes-slavery","american-civil-war","Unlike the [[american-civil-war|American Civil War]], it cost no war, and unlike the British [[slavery-abolition-act|Slavery Abolition Act]] it paid no compensation."],["the-story-of-the-kelly-gang","hollywood-film-industry","It shows how early Australia took to cinema, years before [[hollywood-film-industry|Hollywood]] made features."],["uluburun-shipwreck","mycenaean-greece","The goods came from at least seven cultures, from [[new-kingdom-egypt|Egypt]] and the [[phoenician-cities|Canaanite coast]] to [[mycenaean-greece|Mycenaean Greece]] and Mesopotamia."],["tenmei-famine","laki-eruption","The same year Iceland's [[laki-eruption|Laki eruption]] cooled the northern hemisphere, which may have made matters worse."],["barbary-slave-trade","miguel-de-cervantes","The Spanish writer [[miguel-de-cervantes|Miguel de Cervantes]] spent five years as a captive in Algiers."],["rajatarangini","al-biruni","A century earlier [[al-biruni|al-Biruni]] had complained that Indians paid little attention to the order of events; Kalhana is the great exception."],["sholay","seven-samurai","The story borrows from Hollywood westerns and from [[seven-samurai|Seven Samurai]], set in the rocky country of the Deccan."],["birka","samanid-silver-to-the-baltic","Graves at Birka hold Arab silver coins, Chinese silk and Frankish glass, signs of the eastern routes used by the [[varangians|Varangians]] and of the [[samanid-silver-to-the-baltic|silver that flowed from Central Asia]]."],["jiaozi","john-laws-paper-money","[[john-laws-paper-money|John Law's scheme]] in France in 1716 to 1720 repeated many of the Song's lessons."],["yupa-inscriptions-of-kutai","pallavas","The texts, in [[sanskrit|Sanskrit]] and a southern Indian script related to the [[pallavas|Pallava]] script, praise King [[mulavarman|Mulavarman]] of the kingdom later called [[kutai-martadipura|Kutai Martadipura]]."],["haber-process","guano-era","Plants need nitrogen to grow, and before this farmers got extra nitrogen mainly from manure, Chilean saltpetre and seabird droppings shipped from Peru in the [[guano-era|Guano Era]]."],["slow-food-movement","mcdonalds","It began as a protest. In 1986 a [[mcdonalds|McDonald's]] opened by the Spanish Steps in Rome, and Petrini's circle answered with a call to eat slowly, together, and well."],["euclid","matteo-ricci","The Elements was copied for centuries, put into Arabic when [[greek-science-to-baghdad|Greek science reached Baghdad]], into Latin in the 12th century, and into Chinese by [[matteo-ricci|Matteo Ricci]] and Xu Guangqi in 1607."],["huguenots-at-the-cape","louis-xiv","They had fled France after [[louis-xiv|Louis XIV]] outlawed Protestantism in 1685 with the [[edict-of-fontainebleau|Edict of Fontainebleau]]."],["mongolian-democratic-revolution","tiananmen-square-protests","Unlike in China a year earlier, at [[tiananmen-square-protests|Tiananmen Square]], no one was shot."],["sintashta-andronovo-cultures","rigveda","Their languages are the likely ancestors of Iranian languages and of the Sanskrit of the [[rigveda|Rigveda]]."],["iliad","phoenician-alphabet","Writing it down was possible because the Greeks had just adapted the [[phoenician-alphabet|Phoenician alphabet]] into the [[greek-alphabet|Greek alphabet]]."],["diamond-sutra-printed","aurel-stein","In 1907 the explorer [[aurel-stein|Aurel Stein]] bought it with many others and took it to London, where it is now in the British Library."],["al-farabi","aristotle","Al-Farabi was a philosopher and music theorist of the early Islamic world, called the \"Second Teacher\", second only to [[aristotle|Aristotle]], the First."],["toledo-school-of-translators","house-of-wisdom","Toledo did for Europe what the [[house-of-wisdom|House of Wisdom]] had done for Baghdad."],["obelisk-of-axum","benito-mussolini","After [[benito-mussolini|Mussolini]]'s army conquered Ethiopia in the [[second-italo-ethiopian-war|Second Italo-Ethiopian War]], Italian soldiers took the stele, which was lying in pieces, to Rome."],["tiberius","jesus","From 26 CE he lived on the island of [[capri|Capri]] and never returned to the city. [[jesus|Jesus]] was crucified in Judaea during his reign."],["kition","zeno-of-citium","Its most famous son was the philosopher [[zeno-of-citium|Zeno]], founder of Stoicism."],["leptis-magna","septimius-severus","Its most famous son, [[septimius-severus|Septimius Severus]], born there in 145, became Roman emperor in 193 and filled his home town with a new forum, a basilica, a harbour and a triumphal arch."],["reggae","windrush-generation","Caribbean migrants of the [[windrush-generation|Windrush generation]] made Britain a second home for it."],["kush-napata-meroe","assyria","His successors, above all [[taharqa|Taharqa]], ruled from Nubia to the Mediterranean and built across both lands. The [[assyria|Assyrians]] drove them out of Egypt by 656 BCE."],["averroes","al-ghazali","He also wrote a medical encyclopedia and a defence of philosophy against the attacks of the theologian [[al-ghazali|al-Ghazali]], arguing that reason and revealed religion cannot truly conflict."],["sol-plaatje","william-shakespeare","His novel Mhudi, set in the wars of the 1830s, appeared in 1930. He also translated [[william-shakespeare|Shakespeare]] into Setswana."],["gur-e-amir","mughal-empire","The Gur-e-Amir became a model for the great tombs of the [[mughal-empire|Mughal Empire]], whose rulers descended from Timur through [[babur|Babur]]."],["bujang-valley","chola-raid-on-srivijaya","The port, known in Indian texts as Kadaram, traded with India, China and the Middle East, and later fell under the power of [[srivijaya|Srivijaya]]. In 1025 the [[chola-raid-on-srivijaya|Chola navy]] of south India raided it."],["bogd-khan-enthroned","xinhai-revolution","Mongol princes had declared independence weeks after the [[xinhai-revolution|Xinhai Revolution]] broke the [[qing|Qing]] dynasty, saying their loyalty had been to the Manchu emperor, not to China."],["maragheh-observatory","nicolaus-copernicus","Similar ideas appear later in the work of [[nicolaus-copernicus|Nicolaus Copernicus]], and historians still debate whether he learned of them."],["ulugh-beg-star-catalogue","tycho-brahe","Its accuracy was not surpassed until Taqi al-Din in Istanbul and [[tycho-brahe|Tycho Brahe]] in Denmark in the late 1500s."],["cleopatra","assassination-of-julius-caesar","She was in Rome when [[assassination-of-julius-caesar|Caesar was murdered]] in 44 BCE."],["egypt-feeds-rome","vespasian","Whoever held Egypt could starve Rome, which is why [[vespasian|Vespasian]] seized it first in his bid for the throne in 69 CE."],["sony","transistor","In the 1950s they licensed the [[transistor|transistor]] from Bell Labs in the United States and put it into small pocket radios, sold around the world from 1957."],["wind-power-in-denmark","1973-oil-embargo","The [[1973-oil-embargo|oil shock of 1973]] hit a country that imported almost all its energy, and a popular movement rejected nuclear power."],["utendi-wa-tambuka","heraclius","Its subject is the early Muslim war against the Byzantine emperor [[heraclius|Heraclius]], set around Tabuk in Arabia, and it tells of the courage and faith of the Prophet's companions in heroic verse."],["sven-hedin","adolf-hitler","He backed Germany in the First World War, and in the 1930s and 1940s he admired [[adolf-hitler|Hitler]] and spoke for the Nazi regime."],["sesame-synchrotron","cern","The project was modelled on [[cern|CERN]], the European physics laboratory founded after World War II partly to bring former enemies together."],["kumarajiva","changan-rebuilt","In 401 the ruler of the Later Qin brought him to [[changan-rebuilt|Chang'an]], gave him honours and a team of hundreds of monks, and he spent his last years translating."],["kuwaiti-dhow-trade","swahili-city-states","Each autumn ships carried dates from [[basra|Basra]] down the Gulf to India, Yemen and the [[swahili-city-states|Swahili coast]], riding the [[monsoon|monsoon]] winds, and came back with timber, spices, rice and cloth."],["mellah","expulsion-of-jews-from-spain","Jews had lived in Morocco since ancient times, and were joined by refugees after the [[expulsion-of-jews-from-spain|expulsion from Spain]] in 1492."],["faras-cathedral-murals","aswan-high-dam","When the [[aswan-high-dam|Aswan High Dam]] was built, a Polish team led by [[kazimierz-michalowski|Kazimierz Michałowski]] dug the cathedral out and cut the paintings off the walls."],["c-v-raman","subrahmanyan-chandrasekhar","His nephew [[subrahmanyan-chandrasekhar|Subrahmanyan Chandrasekhar]], his elder brother's son, won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1983."]];
